      "rules": [
        {
          "body": "Apply when one reusable progress source serves distinct visits and physical attempts, startup may emit cached state synchronously, decoding may complete later or out of order, and audit/history has a different lifetime from visible presentation.",
          "category": "applicability",
          "id": "R01"
        },
        {
          "body": "Install the panel listener before starting a source that may emit cached progress synchronously. Preserve later streaming and the original startup and cleanup interfaces.",
          "category": "event_relation",
          "id": "R02"
        },
        {
          "body": "Decide packet admission for its originating visit/attempt before decoding, including while startup has not yet returned a cleanup capability. Retirement immediately revokes further admission; physical listener removal alone is not the logical lifetime boundary.",
          "category": "event_relation",
          "id": "R03"
        },
        {
          "body": "Assign arrival identity before decoding, and publish only completions newer than the last displayed frame for that originating subscription/attempt. Commit freshness state before callback-capable painting. Compare arrival identity, not numeric loaded values: later full frames may legitimately decrease or reset.",
          "category": "event_relation",
          "id": "R04"
        },
        {
          "body": "Separate admission, retained audit/history, and visible publication. Already-admitted decoding retains its audit/history after retirement or a newer visible frame, while painting must recheck the originating visit and freshness. Reopening the same source creates a distinct visit.",
          "category": "preservation",
          "id": "R05"
        },
        {
          "body": "Establish cleanup ownership before synchronous startup can navigate. Retire old ownership before reentrant cleanup; recheck ownership before installing a returned handle. Never let an outer startup overwrite a newer visit resource. Preserve idempotent removal and cancellation.",
          "category": "preservation",
          "id": "R06"
        },
        {
          "body": "Preserve accepted retry commands and their entry-bound queue records across cancellation callbacks, including navigation during cancellation. Do not add an early return that drops an accepted command merely because the callback navigates.",
          "category": "preservation",
          "id": "R07"
        },
        {
          "body": "Keep the repair scoped to panel reception, admission, ordering and their necessary lifetime coordination. Preserve diagnostic/audit consumer policy and original queue-record shape; do not generalize panel visibility policy to independent consumers.",
          "category": "exclusion",
          "id": "R08"
        },
        {
          "body": "Check warm cached bootstrap and later streaming, reversed decoding with every admitted audit retained, decreasing/reset frames, late completion after departure and same-file reopening. Exercise synchronous hide/switch/dispose during startup and cleanup, multiple startup packets, subsequent-packet rejection, retry cancellation navigation and diagnostic operation after stop.",
          "category": "verification",
          "id": "R09"
        }
      ],
